scholar|researcher|NOUN|Learned academic|Someone with deep knowledge of a subject, often through study and research.|học giả|A visiting scholar gave a lecture on ancient poetry.|Một học giả thỉnh giảng giảng về thơ cổ.|Countable; Master overlap unresolved.|0
thick|dimension|ADJECTIVE|Large distance between surfaces|Having a relatively large distance between opposite surfaces.|dày|The book has a thick cover.|Cuốn sách có bìa dày.|Thickness dimension, not width alone.|0
thick|consistency|ADJECTIVE|Not flowing easily|Having a dense consistency that does not flow easily.|đặc|The soup is thick with lentils.|Súp đặc vì có nhiều đậu lăng.|Thick liquid; contrast thin.|1
sharp|edge|ADJECTIVE|Able to cut or pierce|Having a fine edge or point that cuts or pierces easily.|sắc; nhọn|The scissors have sharp blades.|Kéo có lưỡi sắc.|Sharp edge or point.|0
sharp|change|ADJECTIVE|Sudden and large|Happening suddenly and with a large effect or amount.|đột ngột; mạnh|There was a sharp rise in demand.|Nhu cầu tăng mạnh đột ngột.|Sharp rise, fall, or turn.|1
sharp|pain|ADJECTIVE|Intense pointed pain|Describing sudden intense pain rather than a dull ache.|đau nhói; buốt|She felt a sharp pain in her ankle.|Cô ấy cảm thấy đau nhói ở mắt cá chân.|Pain adjective; no diagnosis.|2
sharp|mind|ADJECTIVE|Quick to notice and understand|Able to notice or understand things quickly.|nhạy bén; tinh tường|His sharp eye spotted the printing error.|Con mắt tinh tường của anh ấy phát hiện lỗi in.|Sharp mind or eye.|3
undergo|experience|VERB|Experience a process|To experience a change, procedure, or process.|trải qua|The building will undergo extensive repairs.|Tòa nhà sẽ được sửa chữa lớn.|Undergo, underwent, undergone; transitive.|0
suspect|verb|VERB|Think something may be true|To think something is probably true without being certain.|nghi ngờ; cho rằng có thể|I suspect the address is outdated.|Tôi nghi địa chỉ đã cũ.|Suspect that; also suspect someone of doing.|0
suspect|person|NOUN|Person suspected of a crime|Someone thought possibly to have committed a crime.|nghi phạm|The police interviewed a suspect.|Cảnh sát phỏng vấn một nghi phạm.|Countable; suspicion does not establish guilt.|1
